UID:10001470-1793613600-1802880000@nchumanities.org
SUMMARY:Building a Mixed Race Community exhibit at the Museum of the Albemarle
DESCRIPTION:Funded by North Carolina Humanities the Chowan Discovery Group\, the exhibit\, “Building a Mixed Race Community – People\, Buildings and Sites of the Winton Triangle” tells of Hertford County landowning people of color for 1851 to 1970. The includes the years of before and during the Civil War\, Reconstruction\, the Jim Crow and Civil Rights eras. The 30-panel\, 75 foot long exhibit is full of photographs and texts. It covers the Winton Triangle’s involvement with family\, worship\, war\, agriculture\, education\, business\, healthcare\, construction and Civil Rights. The exhibit closes February 24\, 2027. For more information\, contact marvin@chowandiscovery and visit www.chowandiscovery.org.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/building-a-mixed-race-community-exhibit-at-the-museum-of-the-albemarle/
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle\, 501 South Water Street\, Elizabeth City\, NC\, 27909\, United States
CATEGORIES:NC Humanities Grantee Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/MarvinTupperJones_PanelGroupPhotographs_012d-12INCH-72.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Chowan Discovery Group":MAILTO:marvin@chowandiscovery.org
GEO:36.2965317;-76.219757
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Museum of the Albemarle 501 South Water Street Elizabeth City NC 27909 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=501 South Water Street:geo:-76.219757,36.2965317
END:VEVENT
